1
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:43,900
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,750
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:57,570 --> 00:01:59,289
[Operating Room Anteroom]

4
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,640
Sterile gauze.

5
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,640
Coming.

6
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:07,790
Here.

7
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,150
The patient was struck on the left side.

8
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:12,150
When she fell,

9
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,800
the right side of her head hit the ground.

10
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,960
The patient has a depressed fracture
of the left temporal region,

11
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,750
a left-sided cerebral contusion
and laceration,

12
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:20,210
and a small right-sided subdural hematoma.

13
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:23,400
There's a marked midline shift
to the right.

14
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,240
The patient's left pupil

15
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,970
is now significantly dilated.

16
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,380
We need to remove the hematoma on the left

17
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,000
and perform a decompressive craniectomy.

18
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,750
If there are significant changes

19
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:31,840
on the right side,

20
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:32,590
we'll deal with them then.

21
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:34,520
The fracture is at least 10 cm long.

22
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:35,840
How did that happen?

23
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,090
Her husband hit her with a club.

24
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:42,520
What the hell?

25
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,000
Is he even human?

26
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,710
Did anyone call the police?

27
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:45,840
Calm down first.

28
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,560
The patient's family said

29
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,220
the police had taken him away.

30
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:49,990
Keep your emotions

31
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:50,920
out of your work.

32
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:53,840
And what if, after we finish...

33
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:56,630
the pressure on the left side drops,

34
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:57,800
but the bleeding
on the right side increases?

35
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,560
What do we do then?

36
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,620
Povidone-iodine.

37
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,150
If there's significant bleeding
on the right side,

38
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:05,550
we'll have to perform another craniotomy.

39
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:07,080
We'll see whether we can

40
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,000
preserve her bone flaps.

41
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,960
If we can't,

42
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,810
she'll have a big dent
on each side of her head.

43
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,360
How is she supposed to live like that?

44
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,680
This is no time for that.

45
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,810
Save her life first.

46
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:19,760
Nothing matters more than staying alive.

47
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,300
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

48
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,310
The depressed skull fracture

49
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:37,079
caused by the assault

50
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:39,120
has resulted in some adhesion

51
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,079
between the inner surface of the skull
and the dura mater.

52
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:42,360
Separating the bone flap

53
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,310
carries a high risk of causing

54
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:45,800
further damage to the brain tissue
beneath the dura.

55
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,150
I'll use rongeurs to remove

56
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:48,680
the skull fragments first.

57
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,310
Neuro dissector.

58
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,970
The bone flap is off.

59
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:10,690
Now opening the dura further.

60
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,020
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

61
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:26,270
Once we've finished removing the hematoma,

62
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:27,510
we also need to place

63
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:29,510
an intracranial pressure monitor
in the ventricle.

64
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,310
Have you performed
a ventricular puncture before?

65
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:32,070
Yes.

66
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,270
You'll do it later.

67
00:04:36,159 --> 00:04:36,750
But I've never done it

68
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:39,040
on a patient
with such severe brain injuries before.

69
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:39,770
Give it a try.

70
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,159
W-Why aren't you doing it yourself?

71
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:44,760
If you can't, I'll take over.

72
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,720
I followed the trajectory
for ventricular puncture...

73
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,180
the puncture trajectory.

74
00:05:09,430 --> 00:05:10,720
Why isn't any cerebrospinal fluid
coming out?

75
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,980
Think carefully about

76
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:14,970
the patient's
current intracranial condition.

77
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:17,560
There's significant displacement
of the brain tissue.

78
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,720
Shouldn't the direction

79
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,980
of your needle be adjusted accordingly?

80
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,000
The CSF is coming out.

81
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:53,800
That's good.

82
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:02,650
[Beijing Time] [Elapsed Time]

83
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:10,810
The left pupil has returned to normal.

84
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,370
The right one is normal.

85
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,480
The intracranial pressure
is still a bit high.

86
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:17,310
To be safe,

87
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:18,510
give her a CT scan.

88
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:22,140
[Emergency; 18]

89
00:06:20,430 --> 00:06:21,070
You do it.

90
00:06:22,390 --> 00:06:23,190
I can't.

91
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:25,160
I haven't been in
an operating room in 2 years.

92
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,360
Call Che Mingming.

93
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,970
Tell her to come over immediately.

94
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,110
Junnan.

95
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:33,830
Junnan!

96
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:37,320
Why are you here?

97
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:39,930
I need to talk to you about something.

98
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,510
The bleeding on the right
has increased significantly.

99
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:44,710
What about the pupil?

100
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,880
The pupil is dilated.

101
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:51,000
Then we'll have to remove the hematoma
on the other side

102
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,270
and perform
a decompressive craniectomy there too.

103
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:54,120
Now she really will have

104
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,780
a dent on each side of her head.

105
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,070
But you're right.

106
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,870
Staying alive matters more than anything.

107
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:00,070
There's no other way.

108
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:01,510
She'll have to wait until she recovers

109
00:07:01,510 --> 00:07:02,830
and then have reconstructive surgery.

110
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:04,760
Prepare to evacuate the hematoma.

111
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,560
Is the angle okay?

112
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:09,310
Yes.

113
00:07:09,870 --> 00:07:11,670
Now irrigate the surgical site.

114
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,630
We need to remove the hematoma

115
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:20,720
and the nonviable brain tissue

116
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,120
from the lacerated brain

117
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:25,360
while protecting
the surrounding brain tissue

118
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,750
that remains
relatively intact and functional.

119
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,360
This requires a higher level of precision

120
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,360
in the operation.

121
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:33,050
Adjust it a bit.

122
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:49,920
You're good at the sing-and-dance duet.

123
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:50,780
Who taught you?

124
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:52,760
I taught myself.

125
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,180
You did a good job just now.

126
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,510
Um, I think you...

127
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,760
have at least a 50% chance

128
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:03,630
of getting into the PhD program.

129
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,720
Only 50%?

130
00:08:06,430 --> 00:08:07,070
Doctors never

131
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:08,390
speak in absolutes.

132
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:11,890
Besides, a 50% chance
is already pretty good.

133
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,510
You're really something.

134
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:15,290
Even your compliments

135
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:16,550
come out sounding off.

136
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:19,430
But...

137
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:20,830
Um,

138
00:08:20,830 --> 00:08:22,690
you still have other advantages.

139
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,950
For example, um...

140
00:08:22,950 --> 00:08:25,990
[No smoking]

141
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:27,160
Enough, enough.

142
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,430
Stop stumbling over your words.

143
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:30,270
I know you're not good at saying thanks

144
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:31,270
or apologizing.

145
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,860
Message received on both counts.

146
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,630
If you have any questions
about the PhD exams,

147
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:38,159
feel free to ask me anytime.

148
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:40,990
Then thank you, Zhengliang!

149
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:42,669
My heart

150
00:08:42,409 --> 00:08:45,200
[Quiet]

151
00:08:43,510 --> 00:08:44,840
is pounding like crazy.

152
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:47,270
Thump, thump, thump.

153
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,440
My mom had

154
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,730
heart problems back in the day.

155
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,270
Do you think I might have...

156
00:08:54,270 --> 00:08:55,750
Don't overthink it. Don't overthink it.

157
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,320
Let me see if I can... try a trick on you.

158
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,840
Why are you w-worrying so much?

159
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,320
Let me see

160
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,080
if I can ease it for you.

161
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,550
Do I need to take any medication?

162
00:09:01,550 --> 00:09:02,480
No need, no need.

163
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,360
My heart is thumping...

164
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:03,820
Come on.

165
00:09:06,030 --> 00:09:07,560
Let's try this. Just relax.

166
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:10,320
You need to calm yourself down first.

167
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,000
Come on. Come on.

168
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,390
Come on, this might feel a little cold.

169
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:14,910
Bear with it. Bear with it.

170
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:15,890
Come on. Come on.

171
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:18,000
Come on, breathe out. Breathe out.

172
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,460
That's it. Now breathe in.

173
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,550
Breathe in. Hold it, hold it.

174
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:23,360
Come on, now breathe out.

175
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,630
There's n-nothing else wrong with you.

176
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:28,490
Nothing at all.

177
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:30,630
Try to manage your emotions.

178
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,550
Come out. I need to talk to you.

179
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:34,480
Perfect timing.

180
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,780
Zhengguang was here earlier.

181
00:09:37,030 --> 00:09:38,760
He asked me to pass on a message.

182
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,360
He wants you to move back home.

183
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,620
He's going to Beijing.

184
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:44,830
What's wrong?

185
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:47,680
Why did you want to become a doctor?

186
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,510
I never wanted to be a doctor.

187
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:52,630
My dad wanted me to be one.

188
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:53,080
Fine.

189
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,670
Then what do you want to do?

190
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,150
I...

191
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,750
I don't know what I want to do.

192
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:00,710
But I know what I don't want to do.

193
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:03,750
I don't want to... perform surgery.

194
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:07,480
Because whenever I step into

195
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:09,080
the operating room, I panic.

196
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,790
Well, if I do surgery on a patient

197
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:11,510
and mess it up,

198
00:10:11,510 --> 00:10:13,320
isn't that the same as harming them?

199
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,080
So you're worried

200
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,240
your skills aren't good enough,

201
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,440
and you're afraid to operate.

202
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,120
On the surface,

203
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,200
it looks like you're thinking about
what's best for the patients

204
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,360
and taking responsibility for them,

205
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,960
but in reality
you're just avoiding the problem.

206
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,270
No, I'm not avoiding anything.

207
00:10:22,270 --> 00:10:23,510
Not every doctor

208
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:25,000
has to perform surgery, right?

209
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,360
Some doctors, like you,

210
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:28,270
are suited to operating.

211
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,510
And someone like me

212
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:30,600
is suited to providing

213
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,400
emotional support to patients.

214
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,720
I just want to work shifts
and prescribe medication.

215
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,380
That's a way of living, right?

216
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,320
Do you think...

217
00:10:51,390 --> 00:10:52,670
I don't deserve to be a doctor?

218
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:53,670
Yes, I do think so.

219
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:23,210
The surgery went as expected.

220
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:25,510
We'll monitor her for a few days.

221
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:26,150
She may

222
00:11:26,150 --> 00:11:28,210
need reconstructive surgery later.

223
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:31,510
How much more will that cost?

224
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,360
Your deposit is enough for now.

225
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:35,950
Once her condition stabilizes,

226
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:38,300
repairing both sides of her skull

227
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:41,990
will cost around 70,000 to 80,000 yuan.

228
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,360
We retired a couple of years ago.

229
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:46,720
At our age,

230
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:48,390
we're still working at a hotel.

231
00:11:48,390 --> 00:11:51,050
We can't come up with
that much money all at once.

232
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,510
But if you don't do it,

233
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,030
she'll have dents

234
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:59,360
on both sides of her head from now on.

235
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,800
It would really affect her appearance.

236
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:18,390
[Family Members Not Allowed]

237
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:41,040
[Family Members Not Allowed]

238
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,450
Is Liu Zhengguang here?

239
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,200
He left a long time ago.

240
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,860
Do you need him for something?

241
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,240
He came to the hospital this afternoon

242
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,790
and asked Chen Junnan
to tell me something.

243
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,450
He said he's going to Beijing.

244
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,140
Do you know why he's going to Beijing?

245
00:13:06,270 --> 00:13:07,800
Why don't you just call him?

246
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,800
Let me think about it.

247
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,560
What's there to think about?

248
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,600
You obviously care about him.

249
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,150
You're brothers. What's so hard about
expressing your feelings?

250
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:17,600
It's not that I care about him.

251
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:17,960
I...

252
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:19,670
I'm just afraid he'll...

253
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:20,720
he'll cause more trouble.

254
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,510
Fine, fine.

255
00:13:22,910 --> 00:13:23,630
I give up.

256
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:24,870
You two are exactly alike—

257
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:26,200
both stubborn as mules.

258
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,770
You're getting off work this late?

259
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:30,840
You're going back alone.

260
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:31,900
Aren't you scared?

261
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,000
Are you worried about me?

262
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,570
Then do you want to walk me home?

263
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,350
We're not that close, are we?

264
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,790
I've still got a shift to finish.

265
00:13:46,790 --> 00:13:47,790
Go back to work!

266
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,720
Why even say it?

267
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,700
D-Don't worry.

268
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,760
I'm not going home alone anyway.

269
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,600
[1314 Funeral Services]

270
00:13:57,390 --> 00:13:59,360
I've been watching you for a while.

271
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,820
You've got your eye on him,

272
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:03,790
and I've got my eye on you.

273
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:14,480
So, Liu Zhengliang...

274
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:16,090
You're serious about him?

275
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:17,200
Yeah.

276
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:20,120
Then how does he feel about you?

277
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,550
Who cares?

278
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,460
I'll win him over sooner or later anyway.

279
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,440
Back then,

280
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,120
was it also Mom who pursued you first?

281
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,270
Not exactly.

282
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:33,320
There were plenty of guys
chasing your mom back then.

283
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,720
Some were richer than me.

284
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,520
Some were more handsome.

285
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,750
Then why did I have the last laugh?

286
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:40,390
That's because

287
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:42,080
I dared to risk my life

288
00:14:42,510 --> 00:14:44,320
for your mom.

289
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:48,870
That bunch...

290
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:51,160
That bunch of young punks chasing her?

291
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,630
I'd beat up every one that showed up.

292
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:53,720
Every single one.

293
00:14:56,510 --> 00:14:58,030
What year do you think this is?

294
00:14:58,030 --> 00:14:59,480
Who still fights like that?

295
00:14:59,480 --> 00:14:59,840
Well,

296
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,910
I mean,

297
00:15:01,550 --> 00:15:03,390
your mom was indeed pretty back then,

298
00:15:03,390 --> 00:15:05,120
but not as pretty as you.

299
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:07,750
A daughter as great as mine

300
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:11,870
deserves a man

301
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:14,120
who'd risk everything for her.

302
00:15:15,910 --> 00:15:16,720
Dad.

303
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,660
I'm your daughter.

304
00:15:21,910 --> 00:15:23,240
If you can give everything

305
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,570
for the person you love,

306
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,630
then so can I.

307
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:34,630
Coming.

308
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:39,840
What's the deal?

309
00:15:40,270 --> 00:15:41,670
You're going to Beijing?

310
00:15:41,910 --> 00:15:42,910
Who told you that?

311
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:43,910
Didn't you ask Chen Junnan

312
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:44,870
to tell me?

313
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,910
I asked him to tell you to move back home,

314
00:15:47,910 --> 00:15:49,970
not to tell you I was going to Beijing.

315
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,530
I don't want to move back right now.

316
00:15:55,270 --> 00:15:56,270
Suit yourself.

317
00:15:57,150 --> 00:15:58,750
I just don't want the apartment
sitting empty and going to waste.

318
00:15:58,750 --> 00:15:59,670
If you don't want to live here,

319
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:00,910
you can live wherever you want.

320
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:02,370
Don't change the subject.

321
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,800
Why are you going to Beijing?

322
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,600
Because I've lived

323
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,000
in Fucheng my whole life.

324
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,100
I want to go out and try my luck!

325
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:14,210
What's that got to do with you?

326
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,150
Mind your own business.

327
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:16,880
Who said I was going to stop you?

328
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,150
Just do me a favor and let me know

329
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,150
when you leave.

330
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:21,720
I'll move back in after you leave.

331
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:22,580
I'm off to work.

332
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,890
Liu Zhengliang!

333
00:16:29,550 --> 00:16:31,480
Aren't you afraid I won't find a job

334
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:32,960
and will starve to death out there?

335
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:33,840
What if I end up

336
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,670
sleeping on the streets
and turning to crime?

337
00:16:35,670 --> 00:16:37,000
What if I commit a crime?

338
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:40,120
What are you laughing at?

339
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,050
Liu Zhengguang,

340
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,720
stop making me laugh.

341
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:44,720
"Startup Dreams:
Beijing, Shanghai & Guangzhou"—

342
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:46,510
[Startup Dreams:
Beijing, Shanghai & Guangzhou]

343
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,120
can you even follow this?

344
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,840
And turning to crime?

345
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:49,550
Do you even have the guts?

346
00:16:50,670 --> 00:16:51,750
Who do you think you're looking down on?

347
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:53,120
Come back if you can't make it.

348
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:53,790
Call me if you can't

349
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:54,600
afford a ticket.

350
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,870
Otherwise, don't contact me.

351
00:16:55,870 --> 00:16:56,840
Listen here, Liu Zhengliang.

352
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:57,790
I definitely won't call you.

353
00:16:57,790 --> 00:16:59,270
I definitely won't contact you.

354
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:00,150
I'm telling you,

355
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:01,030
I have plenty of people I can turn to.

356
00:17:01,030 --> 00:17:02,030
I can call Ai Chen,

357
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:03,670
Jia Xin, Cai Zhuzi,

358
00:17:03,670 --> 00:17:05,400
Chen Junnan, Che Mingming,

359
00:17:05,510 --> 00:17:07,240
my Uncle Dong, or even old Wu next door!

360
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,700
I'd call any of them
before I'd ever call you!

361
00:17:17,349 --> 00:17:18,160
Mingming.

362
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,480
Thanks. Thanks for the coffee.

363
00:17:22,069 --> 00:17:23,069
Don't mention it.

364
00:17:25,030 --> 00:17:26,359
Are you feeling better?

365
00:17:26,589 --> 00:17:28,050
I'm not upset or anything.

366
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,720
Liu Zhengliang can be

367
00:17:35,030 --> 00:17:37,110
pretty harsh with his words sometimes,

368
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,910
and what he says can really hurt.

369
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,680
But...

370
00:17:41,790 --> 00:17:43,720
it's not because he's wrong.

371
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,400
It's precisely

372
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,400
because he's usually right.

373
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:51,790
I know.

374
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,260
But how does it affect him
if I just coast?

375
00:17:59,070 --> 00:17:59,960
Exactly.

376
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,590
It's because you can't affect him

377
00:18:01,590 --> 00:18:03,850
that he's genuinely looking out for you.

378
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:05,110
What he means is,

379
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,310
either

380
00:18:06,310 --> 00:18:08,310
you work hard to improve your skills

381
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,270
or you change careers ASAP.

382
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:11,830
Just find something you enjoy

383
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:12,960
and are good at.

384
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,070
Wouldn't that be better?

385
00:18:14,070 --> 00:18:15,000
Don't you think?

386
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:22,030
You could put it that way.

387
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,030
I actually think

388
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,160
he is more of

389
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,590
a Northeasterner than many people

390
00:18:31,590 --> 00:18:32,520
who grew up here.

391
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,790
Unlike some people who seem

392
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,640
generous and genuine on the surface

393
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:37,880
but are all

394
00:18:38,110 --> 00:18:39,440
just putting on a show.

395
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,840
You're quite a good judge of character.

396
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:48,840
Which newly divorced woman

397
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,410
wouldn't be clear-headed?

398
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,040
What is this?

399
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,110
Sweet potatoes?

400
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:12,960
What?

401
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,720
Trying to apologize to me
with sweet potatoes?

402
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,790
What are you talking about?

403
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,390
Why would I apologize to you?

404
00:19:18,030 --> 00:19:19,160
Are there any for me?

405
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:20,440
I don't want any.

406
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,040
I bought two. You guys share.

407
00:19:22,110 --> 00:19:23,770
I checked him over. He's fine.

408
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:25,200
Mingming.

409
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:27,880
-What are you three eating?
-Thank you, Zhengliang.

410
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:28,920
Leaving me out, huh?

411
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,250
I didn't buy any for you.

412
00:19:32,470 --> 00:19:33,240
So blunt.

413
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,440
I don't want any. I...

414
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,680
I get heartburn if I eat too much.

415
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:40,310
Come on.

416
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:42,280
Help me finish some of this.

417
00:19:43,070 --> 00:19:45,200
Mingming gave it to me. I have to eat it.

418
00:19:48,070 --> 00:19:48,680
Come on.

419
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:50,480
Help me eat some.

420
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:51,980
I said I don't want any.

421
00:19:52,070 --> 00:19:53,070
Come on.

422
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:54,200
Just try a piece.

423
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,100
Is it sweet?

424
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:08,160
Sweet or not?

425
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:08,880
Is it sweet?

426
00:20:10,550 --> 00:20:12,080
Say something. Is it sweet?

427
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:16,200
Really sweet. Super sweet.

428
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,000
Super sweet.

429
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:19,600
It must be from the old man
at the entrance.

430
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,350
-I can tell by the taste it's from him.
-Doctor!

431
00:20:24,350 --> 00:20:25,110
Doctor!

432
00:20:29,510 --> 00:20:32,110
Jiao... Jiao woke up.

433
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:45,880
Jiao?

434
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:47,680
Jiao?

435
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:49,550
The penlight.

436
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:01,720
Has Jiao shown any signs

437
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,320
of voluntary limb movement?

438
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:04,960
-No.
-No.

439
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,840
Then it seems Jiao...

440
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,820
hasn't regained consciousness.

441
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:12,400
No way.

442
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:13,510
I-I saw her

443
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:14,640
open her eyes.

444
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:16,550
Zhang.

445
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,290
You saw it too, didn't you?

446
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:19,510
Tell the doctors.

447
00:21:19,510 --> 00:21:20,000
Yes.

448
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,680
Tell them I wasn't making it up!
-Yes, I saw it too.

449
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,810
She opened her eyes!

450
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:28,790
That was
an involuntary neurological reflex.

451
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,200
It's fairly common.

452
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:31,680
It can't be taken as

453
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,680
proof that the patient has woken up.

454
00:21:48,590 --> 00:21:49,550
Dr. Liu,

455
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:51,880
is it a good sign

456
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,860
that Jiao opened her eyes?

457
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
She's never opened her eyes before.

458
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,650
Sometimes, hopes do come true.

459
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:03,720
So I...

460
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:06,680
told my first lie

461
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:07,920
as a doctor.

462
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:08,720
Yes.

463
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:10,890
It's a good sign.

464
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,920
It means Jiao's

465
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:15,640
chances of regaining consciousness

466
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,500
have improved.

467
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:19,640
Are you telling the truth?

468
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:23,070
Yes. Yes.

469
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:24,920
So,

470
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:26,270
whenever you have time,

471
00:22:26,270 --> 00:22:27,270
try talking to her more.

472
00:22:27,270 --> 00:22:28,160
It will help.

473
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,110
If anything similar

474
00:22:29,110 --> 00:22:30,310
happens again,

475
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,790
call us anytime.

476
00:22:31,790 --> 00:22:33,270
Okay, okay.

477
00:22:33,550 --> 00:22:35,110
Okay, okay.

478
00:22:35,110 --> 00:22:36,720
Thank you. Thank you.

479
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,330
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

480
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:01,200
Involuntary neurological reflexes

481
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:01,790
have nothing to do with

482
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:02,960
the probability of
regaining consciousness.

483
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,640
You're giving
Zhang Jiao's parents hope now.

484
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:05,830
If Jiao really doesn't wake up,

485
00:23:05,830 --> 00:23:07,680
they will be even more desperate.

486
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:09,270
They just

487
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:10,400
went through

488
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,200
that emotional roller coaster.

489
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:16,830
Mingming,

490
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:19,200
Zhengliang did the right thing.

491
00:23:19,350 --> 00:23:20,550
If he hadn't said something reassuring,

492
00:23:20,550 --> 00:23:23,150
that couple
wouldn't have been able to hold on.

493
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:26,740
[Friendly Reminder]

494
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,830
So he can tell

495
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:34,360
comforting lies after all.

496
00:23:57,830 --> 00:23:59,790
Dad, you had a night shift too?

497
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:01,110
I just got back.

498
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:11,920
Son, you're back.

499
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:12,790
I'm back.

500
00:24:12,790 --> 00:24:13,830
You and your dad should get some sleep.

501
00:24:13,830 --> 00:24:15,000
I'm off to work.

502
00:24:17,510 --> 00:24:18,310
Well,

503
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,200
let me get you 2 boxes of milk.

504
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:21,510
No need.

505
00:24:21,510 --> 00:24:22,400
You already have one.

506
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:23,240
Is one box enough?

507
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:23,830
Yeah.

508
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:36,830
I'm telling you,

509
00:24:36,830 --> 00:24:38,030
wonders never cease.

510
00:24:38,030 --> 00:24:38,590
What's wrong?

511
00:24:38,590 --> 00:24:40,350
Our son has suddenly started
reading books.

512
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:42,030
He's finally trying to improve himself.

513
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:43,440
Seriously, it's been so many years.

514
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,440
I've never seen

515
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,160
him read at home.

516
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,680
He only started reading now?

517
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,030
It's already too late.

518
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,310
Well, aren't you starting to read too?

519
00:24:52,310 --> 00:24:53,400
How old are you?

520
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:54,400
And it's not too late for you?

521
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:55,930
Because I'm getting older,

522
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:57,640
I have to hurry up and read now.

523
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,110
Look at Liu Zhengliang. He's so young,

524
00:24:59,110 --> 00:25:01,370
and his skills are about to surpass mine.

525
00:25:06,830 --> 00:25:08,400
I really can't get into it.

526
00:25:16,510 --> 00:25:22,760
[Mingming] [Are you home?]

527
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,300
[Are you asleep?]

528
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:34,600
[Mingming]

529
00:25:34,650 --> 00:25:38,100
[Are you studying?]

530
00:25:43,190 --> 00:25:54,880
[Are you studying?]

531
00:25:54,970 --> 00:26:02,030
[Chen Junnan]

532
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:08,760
[Sleeping. Do not disturb.]

533
00:26:25,270 --> 00:26:28,550
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

534
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:30,000
Squeeze hard. Squeeze.

535
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:31,750
Right.

536
00:26:32,270 --> 00:26:33,070
Okay.

537
00:26:33,790 --> 00:26:35,350
Come on, lift this leg.

538
00:26:35,350 --> 00:26:36,000
Xiaomei.

539
00:26:35,380 --> 00:26:38,750
[Nurses' Station]

540
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,400
Give me the last patient's medical record.

541
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,060
This one, this one.

542
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:48,590
Okay, this one.

543
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,750
Come on, this leg, lift.

544
00:26:52,070 --> 00:26:52,880
Okay.

545
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:53,720
Cui Jia.

546
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,880
This is Cui Jia.

547
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:57,790
She was hit on the head with a club,

548
00:26:58,240 --> 00:27:00,550
resulting in
an open traumatic brain injury.

549
00:27:00,550 --> 00:27:01,350
Take a look.

550
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:03,520
Her recovery has been pretty good.

551
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:04,270
Dr. Liu

552
00:27:04,270 --> 00:27:05,790
removed the hematoma very thoroughly

553
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:07,680
and preserved her brain tissue quite well.

554
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:08,350
So far,

555
00:27:08,350 --> 00:27:10,720
she hasn't shown any signs
of lasting complications.

556
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:11,510
Doctor.

557
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:13,830
Will I need

558
00:27:13,830 --> 00:27:15,310
reconstructive surgery?

559
00:27:16,790 --> 00:27:18,320
We'd do it in about 3 months.

560
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,880
We'd use a titanium mesh

561
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:21,070
or PEEK material

562
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:22,480
to repair your skull.

563
00:27:22,550 --> 00:27:23,960
I don't want the surgery.

564
00:27:25,790 --> 00:27:28,050
When's the earliest I can be discharged?

565
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,110
At the earliest,

566
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,830
you can be discharged next week.

567
00:27:33,830 --> 00:27:34,920
The skull reconstruction surgery

568
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,120
is entirely up to you.

569
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:37,030
My child,

570
00:27:37,110 --> 00:27:38,310
the doctor said

571
00:27:38,310 --> 00:27:39,200
if you don't get the surgery,

572
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:41,000
you'll have 2 dents on your head.

573
00:27:41,350 --> 00:27:42,160
From a distance,

574
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,550
you'll look like a gourd.

575
00:27:43,550 --> 00:27:45,210
When you walk down the street,

576
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:46,270
won't people

577
00:27:46,270 --> 00:27:47,550
think you're an alien?

578
00:27:47,550 --> 00:27:48,200
Mom.

579
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:53,310
You think I want to skip the surgery?

580
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:57,270
We simply can't afford it.

581
00:27:59,310 --> 00:28:00,440
It's all my fault.

582
00:28:02,750 --> 00:28:03,830
I don't want you

583
00:28:03,830 --> 00:28:05,890
to go further into debt because of me.

584
00:28:11,110 --> 00:28:13,750
The Neurosurgical Department
has been doing well this month.

585
00:28:13,750 --> 00:28:15,270
But there's still room for improvement.

586
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:15,750
Okay.

587
00:28:16,790 --> 00:28:19,120
Take the patient we just saw, for example.

588
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:21,510
We must make sure
she gets her skull reconstruction done

589
00:28:21,510 --> 00:28:22,750
at our hospital.

590
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:24,880
She needs the surgery.

591
00:28:26,110 --> 00:28:27,720
She just hasn't thought it through yet.

592
00:28:27,720 --> 00:28:28,550
If she figures it out later

593
00:28:28,550 --> 00:28:30,210
and goes to another hospital,

594
00:28:30,640 --> 00:28:31,920
it'll be our loss.

595
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:32,400
Yes.

596
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:38,920
Goodbye, President.

597
00:28:41,380 --> 00:28:44,960
[Quiet]

598
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:43,270
I'll leave this to you.

599
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:45,190
Make sure you get it done.

600
00:28:45,510 --> 00:28:46,750
Didn't I just say

601
00:28:46,790 --> 00:28:47,720
it's her choice?

602
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,330
She will choose to do it.

603
00:28:49,750 --> 00:28:51,350
We'll make sure it gets done.

604
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:52,320
Good luck.

605
00:28:52,830 --> 00:28:54,550
I'll go withdraw all 6,000 yuan

606
00:28:54,550 --> 00:28:55,510
from the card.

607
00:28:55,590 --> 00:28:57,850
You go borrow some more from her Aunt Sun.

608
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:04,830
The president is right.

609
00:29:04,830 --> 00:29:06,560
She needs the reconstruction.

610
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,750
She'll have to get the surgery
sooner or later.

611
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:10,590
Most of the cost is
for the medical materials.

612
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:11,750
The hospital doesn't
make much profit from it.

613
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:13,590
So we're not making money
at the patient's expense.

614
00:29:13,590 --> 00:29:15,000
Besides, it'll be cheaper for her

615
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,720
to have it done here
than at other hospitals.

616
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:17,510
I don't care.

617
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:18,960
You made the promise,

618
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,220
so you go persuade her.

619
00:29:22,590 --> 00:29:24,070
The key is to find out

620
00:29:24,070 --> 00:29:24,960
if her family can actually

621
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:25,960
afford it.

622
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:27,070
What if

623
00:29:27,070 --> 00:29:28,920
they're truly at the end of their rope?

624
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:31,640
No matter how hard we try to
persuade them, it won't work.

625
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:33,370
Medical care is not a business.

626
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:35,640
But doctors

627
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:37,240
have to make a living, right?

628
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:38,720
Excuse me,

629
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:39,790
which way

630
00:29:39,790 --> 00:29:40,790
to Cui Jia's ward?

631
00:29:44,380 --> 00:29:47,290
[Divorce Agreement]

632
00:29:45,110 --> 00:29:46,910
I've signed the divorce papers.

633
00:29:48,550 --> 00:29:49,950
You should sign them too.

634
00:29:51,070 --> 00:29:52,800
There's no point in carrying on

635
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:54,510
like this.

636
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,350
I've squandered all your money.

637
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,600
I don't want any compensation from you.

638
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:04,510
I told the judge

639
00:30:05,750 --> 00:30:06,810
that I forgave you.

640
00:30:08,830 --> 00:30:11,230
But let's not
hold each other back anymore.

641
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,200
You need

642
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:17,660
a good woman
who knows how to run a household.

643
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:19,200
I'm not.

644
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:22,720
I'm going to the South to try my luck,

645
00:30:23,550 --> 00:30:24,880
to see

646
00:30:26,270 --> 00:30:27,800
where my limits really lie.

647
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:32,500
He's not going to hit her again, is he?

648
00:30:33,070 --> 00:30:34,640
Don't goad him anymore.

649
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:35,770
Just watch quietly.

650
00:30:37,550 --> 00:30:38,640
I was wrong.

651
00:30:38,830 --> 00:30:40,230
I shouldn't have hit you.

652
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,480
If you want a divorce, fine.

653
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:43,210
I'll even accept going to jail.

654
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,840
Can you just settle down?

655
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:47,960
I won't spend my whole life

656
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:49,310
holed up in this dump.

657
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,440
I'm so beautiful.

658
00:30:53,790 --> 00:30:55,920
Is this really all life has to offer me?

659
00:30:58,510 --> 00:31:00,070
I don't accept it.

660
00:31:05,970 --> 00:31:09,320
[Pizza Hut]

661
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,830
Try this. Double cheese.

662
00:31:14,830 --> 00:31:15,440
Thank you.

663
00:31:15,750 --> 00:31:17,070
You ordered too much.
We can't finish this.

664
00:31:17,070 --> 00:31:18,930
Let's have a taste of everything.

665
00:31:21,110 --> 00:31:22,550
Speaking of Cui Jia,

666
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:24,750
at 16 or 17,

667
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:27,110
she was already hanging around
with a gangster.

668
00:31:27,110 --> 00:31:28,200
That gangster

669
00:31:28,830 --> 00:31:29,880
was young and hot-blooded,

670
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:30,790
always getting into fights.

671
00:31:30,790 --> 00:31:32,520
She fell for him at first sight.

672
00:31:35,350 --> 00:31:36,680
Don't go! Don't go!

673
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:37,350
Just you wait. This is not over.

674
00:31:36,740 --> 00:31:38,290
[Xingyi Hotel]

675
00:31:37,350 --> 00:31:38,030
Wait here, you!

676
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:38,590
Wait here!

677
00:31:38,290 --> 00:31:43,690
[Jiuyue Hotel]

678
00:31:43,830 --> 00:31:44,890
So, what do you say?

679
00:31:48,270 --> 00:31:49,550
I'll take you as my man.

680
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:52,030
Let's get married.

681
00:31:52,030 --> 00:31:54,720
Cui Jia's ambitions were sky-high.

682
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:55,960
She was always

683
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:57,270
chasing one dubious investment

684
00:31:57,270 --> 00:31:58,400
after another:

685
00:31:59,070 --> 00:32:00,790
massive afforestation projects,

686
00:32:00,790 --> 00:32:02,350
crowdfunded tree planting,

687
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:04,440
ant farming,

688
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:05,960
and...

689
00:32:06,830 --> 00:32:08,160
speculating in silver,

690
00:32:08,310 --> 00:32:09,960
bogus stock-trading platforms,

691
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:12,020
and even so-called national assets.

692
00:32:12,550 --> 00:32:13,750
Back then, that gangster

693
00:32:13,750 --> 00:32:14,550
had made a little money

694
00:32:14,550 --> 00:32:15,550
running a small business.

695
00:32:15,550 --> 00:32:19,270
But no amount of money could
withstand that kind of reckless spending.

696
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:20,720
Plant trees.

697
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:21,790
And it's eco-friendly.

698
00:32:21,790 --> 00:32:23,480
Then our 20,000...

699
00:32:22,940 --> 00:32:24,610
[Plant Trees, Grow Rich]

700
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:25,240
26,600 yuan.

701
00:32:25,350 --> 00:32:26,280
I got here first!

702
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:27,240
I got here first!

703
00:32:28,830 --> 00:32:30,550
I got here first! I got here first!

704
00:32:30,550 --> 00:32:31,640
I want 20 mu!

705
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:33,200
Twenty mu?

706
00:32:33,750 --> 00:32:34,830
How much?

707
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,270
53,200 yuan!

708
00:32:36,310 --> 00:32:37,240
Deal!

709
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:38,790
Is this Yilitong Company?

710
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:41,160
This is Cui Jia!

711
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:43,400
I bought ants from you.

712
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:46,020
Let me tell you,

713
00:32:46,830 --> 00:32:48,350
I've raised them

714
00:32:48,350 --> 00:32:49,790
really well.

715
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:51,350
They've grown so big.

716
00:32:51,830 --> 00:32:53,310
When are you coming to collect them?

717
00:32:53,310 --> 00:32:55,110
It wasn't just his money she lost.

718
00:32:55,110 --> 00:32:56,160
She blew through

719
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:57,590
both her parents' and her in-laws'

720
00:32:57,590 --> 00:32:58,920
retirement funds and savings too.

721
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:00,180
Just give it all to her.

722
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:17,200
All the money's been swindled away.

723
00:33:17,590 --> 00:33:18,720
Let's get a divorce.

724
00:33:19,070 --> 00:33:21,200
How will you survive if you divorce me?

725
00:33:22,110 --> 00:33:23,030
Just make sure

726
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:26,140
you're doing okay on your own.

727
00:33:26,270 --> 00:33:27,270
I asked Cui Jia,

728
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:30,790
"Where do you want to go in the South?

729
00:33:32,150 --> 00:33:33,410
Do you have any plans?"

730
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:37,480
She said, "Once you cross Shanhai Pass,

731
00:33:37,830 --> 00:33:39,360
you're in the South, right?

732
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:41,720
I don't have any plans."

733
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,790
When I heard that,

734
00:33:42,920 --> 00:33:46,050
I thought that blow
didn't even knock any sense into her.

735
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:47,920
She really is infuriating.

736
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:50,720
But still, no matter what,
he shouldn't have hit her.

737
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:51,440
Yes.

738
00:33:51,640 --> 00:33:52,750
Hitting someone is never acceptable.

739
00:33:52,750 --> 00:33:53,420
But every situation

740
00:33:53,420 --> 00:33:54,510
has to have an outcome.

741
00:33:54,510 --> 00:33:55,920
And now there is one.

742
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:57,700
They're divorced,

743
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:59,070
and that gangster is in jail.

744
00:33:59,070 --> 00:34:00,440
And your task

745
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,210
can't be completed either.

746
00:34:03,830 --> 00:34:05,110
Well... Anyway...

747
00:34:07,270 --> 00:34:09,270
her family really has no money left.

748
00:34:10,630 --> 00:34:11,960
From what you said,

749
00:34:12,710 --> 00:34:13,920
I think she'll have a hard time

750
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,030
down south too.

751
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,480
What's the big deal?

752
00:34:17,590 --> 00:34:19,230
These days, nobody starves.

753
00:34:19,630 --> 00:34:21,000
If she can't make it,

754
00:34:21,110 --> 00:34:22,370
she can just come back.

755
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:24,030
The problem is, once she's seen

756
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:26,280
the dazzling splendor of a big city,

757
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:28,510
along with all the struggles
beneath the surface,

758
00:34:28,510 --> 00:34:30,070
her horizons will have broadened.

759
00:34:30,070 --> 00:34:32,270
But if she still can't find her footing,

760
00:34:33,670 --> 00:34:34,870
the harder she works,

761
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:36,710
the more hopeless she might feel.

762
00:34:36,710 --> 00:34:38,150
Once her dreams are shattered

763
00:34:38,150 --> 00:34:40,679
and she finally accepts her fate,
coming back

764
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:44,480
might feel even worse than if she'd
never left in the first place.

765
00:34:44,710 --> 00:34:46,670
Come on, guys, lift it!

766
00:34:50,610 --> 00:34:55,540
[1314; Funeral Wreath & Burial Clothes;
Xiaoximen Branch]

767
00:35:04,630 --> 00:35:05,280
Awesome!

768
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:05,920
Nice!

769
00:35:06,070 --> 00:35:06,550
Nice!

770
00:35:06,760 --> 00:35:08,690
These firecrackers were amazing.

771
00:35:08,760 --> 00:35:09,490
What a blast.

772
00:35:10,030 --> 00:35:10,630
Sis.

773
00:35:10,880 --> 00:35:11,340
That...

774
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:14,030
What does that "branches of red flowers
peeking over the wall" mean?

775
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:16,070
Where does it look red?

776
00:35:17,590 --> 00:35:18,480
Isn't that it?

777
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,550
In the corner,
there are a few plum blossoms.

778
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:23,590
They're the only ones blooming.

779
00:35:23,590 --> 00:35:25,110
And you can tell from far away

780
00:35:25,110 --> 00:35:26,070
that they're not snowflakes.

781
00:35:26,070 --> 00:35:26,710
Why?

782
00:35:27,550 --> 00:35:29,630
Because a hidden fragrance comes drifting.

783
00:35:29,630 --> 00:35:30,360
What?

784
00:35:30,360 --> 00:35:31,510
Do you even know which poem that's from?

785
00:35:31,510 --> 00:35:32,320
I don't know.

786
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,670
Sis, what does our funeral business

787
00:35:34,670 --> 00:35:36,330
have to do with plum blossoms?

788
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,110
Are you staging a coup?

789
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:44,330
I decide what goes on my signboard.

790
00:35:45,070 --> 00:35:46,000
Liu Zhengguang.

791
00:35:47,710 --> 00:35:49,110
Where did you pop up from?

792
00:35:49,110 --> 00:35:50,040
What do you want?

793
00:35:50,630 --> 00:35:52,360
Come here. I need to talk to you.

794
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:55,920
What's there to talk about with you?

795
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,080
Let me ask you.

796
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,400
Are you sure you're going to Beijing?

797
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,190
I'm sure.

798
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:02,150
I've already bought the ticket.

799
00:36:02,150 --> 00:36:03,480
I'm leaving on the 31st.

800
00:36:03,590 --> 00:36:04,880
Why not think it over once more,

801
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:06,230
and be sure before you go?

802
00:36:06,230 --> 00:36:07,030
What's with you?

803
00:36:07,030 --> 00:36:08,710
You change your mind every single day.

804
00:36:08,710 --> 00:36:09,150
That's not

805
00:36:09,150 --> 00:36:11,080
what you were saying a few days ago.

806
00:36:13,070 --> 00:36:14,230
I have a classmate.

807
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:16,320
His younger brother got his PhD this year.

808
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:17,110
He sent out a bunch of resumes,

809
00:36:17,110 --> 00:36:18,800
but in the end,
he still went back to his hometown.

810
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,360
Do you think you're better than him?

811
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:21,630
What's that supposed to mean?

812
00:36:21,630 --> 00:36:23,070
Are you saying
my education isn't good enough

813
00:36:23,070 --> 00:36:25,070
and I won't make it in a big city, huh?

814
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:26,360
Trying to scare me?

815
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:27,320
Let me tell you,

816
00:36:27,510 --> 00:36:28,510
I've met plenty of people

817
00:36:28,510 --> 00:36:29,480
more outstanding than you,

818
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:31,610
and in the end, they all went back home.

819
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,960
And let me tell you something,
Liu Zhengliang.

820
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,710
I've been selling urns since I was a kid.

821
00:36:35,710 --> 00:36:36,400
I've seen more people off

822
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:38,070
to their final resting places
than you've ever met in your life.

823
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:39,070
Just because you couldn't make it
in a big city,

824
00:36:39,070 --> 00:36:41,470
do you think everyone
is as clueless as you?

825
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,360
With your anti-intellectual attitude,

826
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:45,630
you'll never fit in a big city.

827
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:47,490
Why even bother going to Beijing?

828
00:36:49,190 --> 00:36:50,840
Now you're attacking my IQ,

829
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,320
huh?

830
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,860
Saying I have a low IQ, huh?

831
00:36:53,110 --> 00:36:54,110
You have a high IQ.

832
00:36:54,230 --> 00:36:55,110
You're awesome.

833
00:36:55,110 --> 00:36:56,510
Y-You're a real powerhouse.

834
00:36:56,510 --> 00:36:57,070
You're highly educated.

835
00:36:57,070 --> 00:36:59,070
You're good at everything,
and you know everything.

836
00:36:59,070 --> 00:37:00,230
But didn't you get

837
00:37:00,230 --> 00:37:00,840
sent packing back here

838
00:37:00,840 --> 00:37:01,900
from the South too?

839
00:37:02,110 --> 00:37:03,880
A-And now you're lecturing me?

840
00:37:04,150 --> 00:37:04,920
So I'm the only one

841
00:37:04,920 --> 00:37:06,000
you get to look down on, huh?

842
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,460
Are you proud of yourself?

843
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:10,810
You're nothing.

844
00:37:14,230 --> 00:37:15,440
Fine, fine.

845
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:18,550
Do whatever you want.

846
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:19,760
Nobody's stopping you.

847
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:20,510
Psycho.

848
00:37:26,670 --> 00:37:27,600
Liu Zhengliang!

849
00:37:29,550 --> 00:37:30,320
Seriously,

850
00:37:30,320 --> 00:37:31,650
why are you so stubborn?

851
00:37:32,230 --> 00:37:33,490
Just say what you want.

852
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:36,140
Don't you care about Zhengguang?

853
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:38,120
Why can't you just say it nicely?

854
00:37:38,550 --> 00:37:39,630
Just tell him,

855
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:41,630
"I care about you.

856
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:43,030
I'm worried you

857
00:37:43,030 --> 00:37:43,840
won't be able to

858
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:45,400
look after yourself out there." Right?

859
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:46,110
You two are brothers.

860
00:37:46,110 --> 00:37:47,000
What can't you say to each other?

861
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:47,760
Just talk to him nicely.

862
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:49,320
What's it got to do with you?

863
00:37:49,630 --> 00:37:51,430
Who are you to tell me how to talk?

864
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:54,330
Ungrateful again, huh?

865
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:58,050
Then why won't you leave me alone?

866
00:37:58,070 --> 00:37:59,930
Are you a masochist or something?

867
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:05,020
You're asking to get slapped!

868
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:08,150
Who do you think you're talking to?

869
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:09,550
I don't owe you anything.

870
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:11,770
Freaking piece of work.

871
00:38:13,670 --> 00:38:14,480
From now on,

872
00:38:14,590 --> 00:38:16,590
I'd have to be crazy to be nice to you!

873
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:19,360
Look at you, so full of yourself.

874
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:20,190
Such a pain in the ass.

875
00:38:20,190 --> 00:38:21,190
Say one more word,

876
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,690
and I'll knock you flat.

877
00:38:25,150 --> 00:38:26,110
Psycho.

878
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:28,050
Thanks, man.

879
00:38:35,250 --> 00:38:38,400
[Nurses' Station]

880
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:40,280
Miss,

881
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,590
even if you're leaving like this,

882
00:38:41,590 --> 00:38:42,150
shouldn't you

883
00:38:42,150 --> 00:38:43,630
at least let your parents know

884
00:38:43,630 --> 00:38:44,590
and say goodbye?

885
00:38:45,590 --> 00:38:46,400
Yeah.

886
00:38:46,710 --> 00:38:47,920
You have to come back

887
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:49,710
in 3 months

888
00:38:49,710 --> 00:38:51,030
for the skull reconstruction.

889
00:38:51,030 --> 00:38:52,800
Don't worry about the money.

890
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:55,590
We'll do everything we can...

891
00:38:55,590 --> 00:38:57,790
to help you get some of the costs waived.

892
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:59,400
I just look a bit ugly.

893
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:03,900
I don't want to
waste any more of their money.

894
00:39:04,590 --> 00:39:05,400
I can manage.

895
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:06,110
No,

896
00:39:06,230 --> 00:39:07,880
it's not just about your appearance.

897
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:09,230
If someone else gets hurt,

898
00:39:09,230 --> 00:39:10,710
they might just be sore for a while.

899
00:39:10,710 --> 00:39:12,000
But for you, it could be life-threatening.

900
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:13,060
Do you understand?

901
00:39:18,150 --> 00:39:18,840
Right.

902
00:39:19,230 --> 00:39:20,070
Even if you decide not to

903
00:39:20,070 --> 00:39:21,190
have the skull reconstruction,

904
00:39:21,190 --> 00:39:22,190
at least get

905
00:39:22,190 --> 00:39:24,280
a protective cap
for the missing parts of your skull.

906
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:25,000
It would help

907
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:26,060
protect your head.

908
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:38,760
Do you guys think this will work?

909
00:39:41,590 --> 00:39:42,280
This...

910
00:39:48,150 --> 00:39:48,840
Thank you. Thank you.

911
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,320
Are you sure you can manage like this?

912
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:52,480
Even a sprain or fracture
takes 100 days to heal.

913
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:54,280
It's only been
a little over 2 weeks for you.

914
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:55,360
Running around everywhere

915
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:56,360
is too dangerous.

916
00:39:57,030 --> 00:39:58,760
Isn't this a bit too makeshift?

917
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:07,420
Everyone lives their own way.

918
00:40:08,670 --> 00:40:09,710
You can make do

919
00:40:10,590 --> 00:40:12,120
and still live a whole life.

920
00:40:14,150 --> 00:40:15,190
To this day,

921
00:40:15,190 --> 00:40:16,320
I still believe

922
00:40:16,440 --> 00:40:18,320
my best days are ahead of me.

923
00:40:19,070 --> 00:40:20,510
I'm going South to give it a shot.

924
00:40:20,510 --> 00:40:21,630
Once I make some real money,

925
00:40:21,630 --> 00:40:23,510
I'll come back and get my skull fixed.

926
00:40:23,510 --> 00:40:24,320
And then

927
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:25,280
I promise I'll help you all

928
00:40:25,280 --> 00:40:26,080
hit your KPIs!

929
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:27,960
This isn't about money.

930
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:29,070
Yeah.

931
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:34,590
Thanks.

932
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:40,200
Be careful. You must be careful.

933
00:40:40,510 --> 00:40:41,550
Sir, take it slow.

934
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:45,480
Take care!

935
00:40:47,260 --> 00:40:51,320
[Outpatient; Entrance]

936
00:40:47,400 --> 00:40:48,200
Let's go, sir.

937
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,110
She's such a flake.

938
00:40:53,630 --> 00:40:55,190
She can barely take care of herself.

939
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:57,190
How is she going to live from here on?

940
00:40:59,550 --> 00:41:01,150
A girl this funny

941
00:41:01,670 --> 00:41:03,130
won't have terrible luck.

942
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:05,410
Let her try her luck.

943
00:41:06,230 --> 00:41:08,030
I'm even a little envious of her.

944
00:41:11,760 --> 00:41:13,890
I hope she makes something of herself.

945
00:41:16,590 --> 00:41:17,230
I still think

946
00:41:17,230 --> 00:41:19,090
she'd be better off staying here.

947
00:41:21,630 --> 00:41:22,560
Liu Zhengliang.

948
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:28,350
[Outpatient; Entrance]

949
00:41:28,510 --> 00:41:29,840
Dr. Liu.

950
00:41:32,510 --> 00:41:33,280
Dr. Liu.

951
00:41:36,670 --> 00:41:38,760
Let's have a little chat today,

952
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:39,970
heart to heart,

953
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:41,920
straightforwardly and honestly,

954
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:44,580
so we can both walk away
with our dignity intact.

955
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:46,960
But if you try to play games with me...

956
00:41:48,150 --> 00:41:48,760
Huh?

957
00:41:48,760 --> 00:41:50,440
You can go ask around about

958
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,960
what I, Ai San, used to do.

959
00:41:57,670 --> 00:41:59,480
What's your deal...

960
00:42:01,190 --> 00:42:02,920
with our Ai Chen?

961
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,150
Nothing.

962
00:42:09,510 --> 00:42:11,440
You're not being straight with me.

963
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:13,550
We've all seen it.

964
00:42:14,630 --> 00:42:15,510
You...

965
00:42:16,190 --> 00:42:18,650
You've been hitting on
our Ai Chen every day.

966
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:19,760
You're a grown man;

967
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:20,920
just admit it.

968
00:42:21,510 --> 00:42:23,070
I wasn't hitting on her.

969
00:42:23,230 --> 00:42:24,400
I don't like her.

970
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:26,060
What am I supposed to admit to?

971
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:41,880
Our Ai Chen

972
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:44,320
has already started to like you.

973
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:47,000
Who do you think you are

974
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:48,400
to say you don't like her?

975
00:42:49,230 --> 00:42:49,960
Is our girl

976
00:42:49,960 --> 00:42:51,360
not good enough for you?

977
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:55,590
Who is that?

978
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:57,510
That's San.

979
00:43:00,070 --> 00:43:01,070
Which San?

980
00:43:03,510 --> 00:43:04,910
Ai Chen's father, Ai San.

981
00:43:05,280 --> 00:43:06,840
A big-time underworld figure
back in the day.

982
00:43:06,840 --> 00:43:07,670
Very tough.

983
00:43:11,550 --> 00:43:12,590
Zhengliang offended him?
